plus and minus range over the hash in Go map order. With float rounding
the reference is nondeterministic (its golden records only that); the
engine sums in sorted key order (D1).
-- order-plus-floats.hbs --
{{plus a=x b=y c=z}}
-- order-plus-floats.jsonl --
{"x":0.1,"y":0.2,"z":0.3}
{"x":1e16,"y":1,"z":-1e16}
-- order-minus-floats.hbs --
{{minus v a=x b=y c=z}}
-- order-minus-floats.jsonl --
{"v":1,"x":0.1,"y":0.2,"z":0.3}
-- order-plus-ints.hbs --
{{plus a=1 b=2 c=3 d=4 e=5 f=6 g=7 h=8 i=9}}
-- order-plus-mixed-skip.hbs --
{{plus a=x b="2" c="x" d=true e=missing}}
-- order-plus-mixed-skip.jsonl --
{"x":1}
-- order-minus-skip.hbs --
{{minus v a="x" b=missing c=1}}
-- order-minus-skip.jsonl --
{"v":"5"}
{"v":"x"}
{}
-- hash-nil-dropped.hbs --
{{plus a=missing b=1}}|{{and a=missing}}|{{or a=missing}}
-- order-and-or.hbs --
{{and a=x b=y c=z}}|{{or a=x b=y c=z}}
-- order-and-or.jsonl --
{"x":1,"y":0,"z":"s"}
